    "reasoning": "Verified every link in the chain. `packages/site/src/routes.ts:89` defines `const DEVELOPMENT = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development'`, and line 385 is the *only* registration site for `leakTestRoutes` (`grep -rn leakTestRoutes` returns exactly two hits: the import at line 57 and the spread at line 385). `runLeakTest.ts:83` spawns the site with `env: { MOCHI_MEMORY_PROBE: '1', NODE_ENV: 'production', PORT }`, and `serverProcess.ts:37` merges it as `{ ...process.env, ...opts.env }`, so the child's `NODE_ENV` is unconditionally `production` — `DEVELOPMENT` is `false` and `/__leak/server-island` is never registered. I confirmed `packages/site/src/index.ts` passes only that one `routes` map and has no catch-all `fetch`, so the path reaches `composedFetch` and 404s; `captureServerIslandHit()` returns `null` on `!res.ok` (`scripts/leak/routes.ts:41-44`), `runLeakTest.ts:97` therefore builds the ring from `STATIC_ROUTES` alone, and the only signal is a `console.warn` at line 99. The `island:server` hit against `/_mochi/island/:name` is genuinely lost: `LeakIslandPage.svelte` uses `mochi:defer`, whose second fetch is performed by the `ServerIsland` client custom element, so the non-browser `loadGen` never issues it — and `/demos/server-island` in `STATIC_ROUTES` only renders the wrapper. Git history makes it worse, not better: before #338 the harness passed `MODE: 'production'` and inherited `NODE_ENV`, which I verified is `undefined` under `bun run` (no `.env` sets it), so `DEVELOPMENT` was already false — the probe has never worked under this harness. I downgrade HIGH_BUG → BUG: this is a manually-invoked internal harness (`grep test:leak .github/` is empty, so it is not a CI gate), nothing user-facing regresses, and it does emit a warning. The defect and the dead `packages/site/src/leak-test/` directory are real, and the fix the finding proposes mirrors the existing `HEAP_SNAPSHOTS_ENABLED` / profiler-route precedent in the same file."
